{"id":"mahabharata-9-027","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":27,"title":"सप्तविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 27 · Sahadeva kills Shakuni's followers","summary":{"en":"Shakuni with the Gandhara horse attacks the Pandavas, but his men are cut down by Sahadeva and the Pandava heroes. The Gandhara cavalry flees with a terrible cry as the sea tossed by a storm.","kn":"ಗಾಂಧಾರ ಅಶ್ವದಳದೊಡನೆ ಶಕುನಿ ಪಾಂಡವರ ಮೇಲೆ ದಾಳಿ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಸಹದೇವ ಮತ್ತು ಪಾಂಡವ ವೀರರು ಅವನ ಜನರನ್ನು ಕತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಬಿರುಗಾಳಿಗೆ ಕದಡಿದ ಸಮುದ್ರದಂತೆ ಘೋರ ಕೂಗಿನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಗಾಂಧಾರ ಅಶ್ವಪಡೆ ಓಡುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"गान्धार अश्वदल के साथ शकुनि पाण्डवों पर आक्रमण करता है, पर उसके लोग सहदेव और पाण्डव वीरों द्वारा काटे जाते हैं। तूफ़ान से उमड़े समुद्र की तरह भयंकर चीख के साथ गान्धार घुड़सवार भागते हैं।","te":"గాంధార అశ్వదళంతో శకుని పాండవులపై దాడి చేస్తాడు; సహదేవుడు, పాండవ వీరులు అతని వారిని నరుకుతారు. తుఫానుకు కలతబడిన సముద్రంలా భయంకర కేకతో గాంధార అశ్వికులు పారిపోతారు.","ta":"காந்தாரக் குதிரைப்படையுடன் சகுனி பாண்டவரைத் தாக்க, சகதேவனும் பாண்டவ வீரரும் அவன் ஆட்களை வெட்டுகின்றனர். புயலால் கலங்கிய கடல் போல் கொடிய கூச்சலுடன் காந்தாரக் குதிரைப்படை ஓடுகிறது.","ml":"ഗാന്ധാര കുതിരപ്പടയോടൊപ്പം ശകുനി പാണ്ഡവരെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; പക്ഷേ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ ആളുകളെ സഹദേവനും പാണ്ഡവവീരന്മാരും വെട്ടിവീഴ്ത്തുന്നു. കൊടുങ്കാറ്റിലിളകുന്ന കടലുപോലെ ഭയങ്കര നിലവിളിയോടെ ഗാന്ധാര അശ്വസേന ഓടിപ്പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.27; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तस्मिन्प्रवृत्ते संग्रामे नरवाजिगजक्षये ।\nशकुनिः सौबलो राजन्सहदेवं समभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the battle had begun, destroying men, horses and elephants, Shakuni, son of Subala, O king, advanced on Sahadeva."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततोऽस्यापततस्तूर्णं सहदेवः प्रतापवान् ।\nशरौघान्प्रेषयामास पतंगानिव शीघ्रगान् ।\nउलूकश्च रणे भीमं विव्याध दशभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he charged, the mighty Sahadeva quickly sent floods of arrows, swift as locusts, at him; and Uluka in the battle pierced Bhima with ten arrows."}},{"n":3,"text":"शकुनिस्तु महाराज भीमं विद्ध्वा त्रिभिः शरैः ।\nसायकानां नवत्या वै सहदेवमवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni, O great king, pierced Bhima with three arrows and covered Sahadeva with ninety."}},{"n":4,"text":"ते शूराः समरे राजन्समासाद्य परस्परम् ।\nविव्यधुर्निशितैर्बाणैः कङ्कबर्हिणवाजितैः ।\nस्वर्णपुङ्खैः शिलाधौतैरा कर्णात्प्रहितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those heroes, meeting one another in the battle, O king, pierced each other with sharp arrows feathered with heron and peacock plumes, gold-feathered, washed on stone and drawn back to the ear."}},{"n":5,"text":"तेषां चापभुजोत्सृष्टा शरवृष्टिर्विशां पते ।\nआच्छादयद्दिशः सर्वा धाराभिरिव तोयदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The shower of arrows shot from their bows and arms, O lord of the people, covered all the directions as a cloud does with streams of rain."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धो रणे भीमः सहदेवश्च भारत ।\nचेरतुः कदनं संख्ये कुर्वन्तौ सुमहाबलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima and Sahadeva, enraged in the battle, O Bharata, both of great strength, moved about creating carnage."}},{"n":7,"text":"ताभ्यां शरशतैश्छन्नं तद्बलं तव भारत ।\nअन्धकारमिवाकाशमभवत्तत्र तत्र ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your force was covered by the hundreds of arrows from those two, O Bharata, and here and there the sky grew dark."}},{"n":8,"text":"अश्वैर्विपरिधावद्भिः शरच्छन्नैर्विशां पते ।\nतत्र तत्र कृतो मार्गो विकर्षद्भिर्हतान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses ran about covered in arrows, and here and there paths were made by those dragging many of the slain."}},{"n":9,"text":"निहतानां हयानां च सहैव हययोधिभिः ।\nवर्मभिर्विनिकृत्तैश्च प्रासैश्छिन्नैश्च मारिष ।\nसंछन्ना पृथिवी जज्ञे कुसुमैः शबला इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth, O revered one, was covered with slain horses and their riders, with cut armor and broken spears, as if mottled with flowers."}},{"n":10,"text":"योधास्तत्र महाराज समासाद्य परस्परम् ।\nव्यचरन्त रणे क्रुद्धा विनिघ्नन्तः परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The warriors there, O great king, meeting one another, moved about the battle in anger, killing one another."}},{"n":11,"text":"उद्वृत्तनयनै रोषात्संदष्टौष्ठपुटैर्मुखैः ।\nसकुण्डलैर्मही छन्ना पद्मकिञ्जल्कसंनिभैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ground was strewn with faces with eyes rolled up in rage and lips bitten tight, wearing earrings, like the filaments of lotuses."}},{"n":12,"text":"भुजैश्छिन्नैर्महाराज नागराजकरोपमैः ।\nसाङ्गदैः सतनुत्रैश्च सासिप्रासपरश्वधैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was strewn too with severed arms, O great king, like the trunks of elephant kings, with armlets and armor, still holding swords, spears and axes."}},{"n":13,"text":"कबन्धैरुत्थितैश्छिन्नैर्नृत्यद्भिश्चापरैर्युधि ।\nक्रव्यादगणसंकीर्णा घोराभूत्पृथिवी विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"With headless trunks rising and others dancing in the fight, the earth, O lord, became dreadful, crowded with flocks of flesh-eaters."}},{"n":14,"text":"अल्पावशिष्टे सैन्ये तु कौरवेयान्महाहवे ।\nप्रहृष्टाः पाण्डवा भूत्वा निन्यिरे यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When only a little of the army was left, the Pandavas, rejoicing, sent the Kauravas to Yama's abode in that great battle."}},{"n":15,"text":"एतस्मिन्नन्तरे शूरः सौबलेयः प्रतापवान् ।\nप्रासेन सहदेवस्य शिरसि प्राहरद्भृशम् ।\nस विह्वलो महाराज रथोपस्थ उपाविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meanwhile the brave and mighty son of Subala struck Sahadeva hard on the head with a spear, and he, dazed, O great king, sank down on his chariot seat."}},{"n":16,"text":"सहदेवं तथा दृष्ट्वा भीमसेनः प्रतापवान् ।\nसर्वसैन्यानि संक्रुद्धो वारयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Sahadeva so, the mighty Bhimasena, enraged, held back all the armies, O Bharata."}},{"n":17,"text":"निर्बिभेद च नाराचैः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ।\nविनिर्भिद्याकरोच्चैव सिंहनादमरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced them with iron arrows by hundreds and thousands, and having pierced them, tamer of foes, gave a lion's roar."}},{"n":18,"text":"तेन शब्देन वित्रस्ताः सर्वे सहयवारणाः ।\nप्राद्रवन्सहसा भीताः शकुनेश्च पदानुगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Terrified by that sound, all the horses and elephants and Shakuni's foot followers fled suddenly in fear."}},{"n":19,"text":"प्रभग्नानथ तान्दृष्ट्वा राजा दुर्योधनोऽब्रवीत् ।\nनिवर्तध्वमधर्मज्ञा युध्यध्वं किं सृतेन वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them broken, King Duryodhana said: \"Turn back, you who do not know dharma! What use is your running away?"}},{"n":20,"text":"इह कीर्तिं समाधाय प्रेत्य लोकान्समश्नुते ।\nप्राणाञ्जहाति यो वीरो युधि पृष्ठमदर्शयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The hero who gives up his life in battle without showing his back wins glory here and the worlds beyond.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"एवमुक्तास्तु ते राज्ञा सौबलस्य पदानुगाः ।\nपाण्डवानभ्यवर्तन्त मृत्युं कृत्वा निवर्तनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed so by the king, those followers of Shakuni turned back against the Pandavas, making death their refuge in turning back."}},{"n":22,"text":"द्रवद्भिस्तत्र राजेन्द्र कृतः शब्दोऽतिदारुणः ।\nक्षुब्धसागरसंकाशः क्षुभितः सर्वतोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they ran in, O king of kings, a terrible noise arose, stirred on all sides like a churning ocean."}},{"n":23,"text":"तांस्तदापततो दृष्ट्वा सौबलस्य पदानुगान् ।\nप्रत्युद्ययुर्महाराज पाण्डवा विजये वृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those followers of Shakuni charging, the Pandavas, set on victory, went to meet them, O great king."}},{"n":24,"text":"प्रत्याश्वस्य च दुर्धर्षः सहदेवो विशां पते ।\nशकुनिं दशभिर्विद्ध्वा हयांश्चास्य त्रिभिः शरैः ।\nधनुश्चिच्छेद च शरैः सौबलस्य हसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Recovering, the unassailable Sahadeva, O lord of the people, pierced Shakuni with ten arrows and his horses with three, and, as if laughing, cut Shakuni's bow with arrows."}},{"n":25,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय शकुनिर्युद्धदुर्मदः ।\nविव्याध नकुलं षष्ट्या भीमसेनं च सप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shakuni, wild for battle, took up another bow and pierced Nakula with sixty arrows and Bhimasena with seven."}},{"n":26,"text":"उलूकोऽपि महाराज भीमं विव्याध सप्तभिः ।\nसहदेवं च सप्तत्या परीप्सन्पितरं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Uluka too, O great king, pierced Bhima with seven arrows and Sahadeva with seventy, trying to protect his father in the battle."}},{"n":27,"text":"तं भीमसेनः समरे विव्याध निशितैः शरैः ।\nशकुनिं च चतुःषष्ट्या पार्श्वस्थांश्च त्रिभिस्त्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena pierced him in the battle with sharp arrows, Shakuni with sixty-four, and the men at his side with three each."}},{"n":28,"text":"ते हन्यमाना भीमेन नाराचैस्तैलपायितैः ।\nसहदेवं रणे क्रुद्धाश्छादयञ्शरवृष्टिभिः ।\nपर्वतं वारिधाराभिः सविद्युत इवाम्बुदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by Bhima's oil-sharpened iron arrows, they in rage covered Sahadeva in the battle with showers of arrows, as clouds with lightning cover a mountain with streams of water."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततोऽस्यापततः शूरः सहदेवः प्रतापवान् ।\nउलूकस्य महाराज भल्लेनापाहरच्छिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as Uluka charged, the brave and mighty Sahadeva cut off his head with a broad-headed arrow, O great king."}},{"n":30,"text":"स जगाम रथाद्भूमिं सहदेवेन पातितः ।\nरुधिराप्लुतसर्वाङ्गो नन्दयन्पाण्डवान्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Felled by Sahadeva, he fell from his chariot to the ground, his whole body drenched in blood, delighting the Pandavas in the battle."}},{"n":31,"text":"पुत्रं तु निहतं दृष्ट्वा शकुनिस्तत्र भारत ।\nसाश्रुकण्ठो विनिःश्वस्य क्षत्तुर्वाक्यमनुस्मरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his son killed there, O Bharata, Shakuni sighed with a tear-choked throat, remembering the words of Kshattri."}},{"n":32,"text":"चिन्तयित्वा मुहूर्तं स बाष्पपूर्णेक्षणः श्वसन् ।\nसहदेवं समासाद्य त्रिभिर्विव्याध सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After thinking for a moment, sighing with eyes full of tears, he approached Sahadeva and pierced him with three arrows."}},{"n":33,"text":"तानपास्य शरान्मुक्ताञ्शरसंघैः प्रतापवान् ।\nसहदेवो महाराज धनुश्चिच्छेद संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Warding off the arrows that were shot with floods of his own, the mighty Sahadeva, O great king, cut Shakuni's bow in the battle."}},{"n":34,"text":"छिन्ने धनुषि राजेन्द्र शकुनिः सौबलस्तदा ।\nप्रगृह्य विपुलं खड्गं सहदेवाय प्राहिणोत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the bow was cut, O king of kings, Shakuni, son of Subala, took up a huge sword and hurled it at Sahadeva."}},{"n":35,"text":"तमापतन्तं सहसा घोररूपं विशां पते ।\nद्विधा चिच्छेद समरे सौबलस्य हसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that dreadful sword flew suddenly at him, O lord of the people, Sahadeva, as if laughing, cut it in two in the battle."}},{"n":36,"text":"असिं दृष्ट्वा द्विधा छिन्नं प्रगृह्य महतीं गदाम् ।\nप्राहिणोत्सहदेवाय सा मोघा न्यपतद्भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the sword cut in two, Shakuni took up a great mace and hurled it at Sahadeva, but it fell uselessly to the ground."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततः शक्तिं महाघोरां कालरात्रिमिवोद्यताम् ।\nप्रेषयामास संक्रुद्धः पाण्डवं प्रति सौबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, enraged, Shakuni sent a terrible spear at the Pandava, raised like the night of Time."}},{"n":38,"text":"तामापतन्तीं सहसा शरैः काञ्चनभूषणैः ।\nत्रिधा चिच्छेद समरे सहदेवो हसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As it came suddenly, Sahadeva, as if laughing, cut it in three in the battle with gold-adorned arrows."}},{"n":39,"text":"सा पपात त्रिधा छिन्ना भूमौ कनकभूषणा ।\nशीर्यमाणा यथा दीप्ता गगनाद्वै शतह्रदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cut in three, that gold-adorned spear fell to the ground like a blazing flash of lightning breaking up in the sky."}},{"n":40,"text":"शक्तिं विनिहतां दृष्ट्वा सौबलं च भयार्दितम् ।\nदुद्रुवुस्तावकाः सर्वे भये जाते ससौबलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the spear destroyed and Shakuni afflicted with fear, all your men fled in the fear that arose, Shakuni's men with them."}},{"n":41,"text":"अथोत्क्रुष्टं महद्ध्यासीत्पाण्डवैर्जितकाशिभिः ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रास्ततः सर्वे प्रायशो विमुखाभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a great shout went up from the Pandavas, joyful in their victory, and nearly all the Dhartarashtras turned their faces away."}},{"n":42,"text":"तान्वै विमनसो दृष्ट्वा माद्रीपुत्रः प्रतापवान् ।\nशरैरनेकसाहस्रैर्वारयामास संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them dispirited, the mighty son of Madri held them back in the battle with many thousands of arrows."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततो गान्धारकैर्गुप्तं पृष्ठैरश्वैर्जये धृतम् ।\nआससाद रणे यान्तं सहदेवोऽथ सौबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in the battle Sahadeva reached Shakuni as he was going away, guarded by Gandhara horsemen and a rear force of horses, holding his hope of victory."}},{"n":44,"text":"स्वमंशमवशिष्टं स संस्मृत्य शकुनिं नृप ।\nरथेन काञ्चनाङ्गेन सहदेवः समभ्ययात् ।\nअधिज्यं बलवत्कृत्वा व्याक्षिपन्सुमहद्धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Remembering the part that remained for him to do, O king, Sahadeva went at Shakuni in his gold-ornamented chariot, drawing his huge bow strongly to the string and shaking it."}},{"n":45,"text":"स सौबलमभिद्रुत्य गृध्रपत्रैः शिलाशितैः ।\nभृशमभ्यहनत्क्रुद्धस्तोत्त्रैरिव महाद्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rushing at Shakuni, in anger he struck him hard with vulture-feathered arrows whetted on stone, as one strikes a great elephant with goads."}},{"n":46,"text":"उवाच चैनं मेधावी निगृह्य स्मारयन्निव ।\nक्षत्रधर्मे स्थितो भूत्वा युध्यस्व पुरुषो भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise man held him in check and said, as if reminding him: \"Stand by your kshatriya dharma and fight; be a man!"}},{"n":47,"text":"यत्तदा हृष्यसे मूढ ग्लहन्नक्षैः सभातले ।\nफलमद्य प्रपद्यस्व कर्मणस्तस्य दुर्मते ॥","meaning":{"en":"You fool, you who rejoiced then in the assembly hall, gambling with dice, take the fruit today of that deed, wicked-minded man!"}},{"n":48,"text":"निहतास्ते दुरात्मानो येऽस्मानवहसन्पुरा ।\nदुर्योधनः कुलाङ्गारः शिष्टस्त्वं तस्य मातुलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those wicked ones who once mocked us are dead. Duryodhana, the coal of his family, is left, and you, his maternal uncle."}},{"n":49,"text":"अद्य ते विहनिष्यामि क्षुरेणोन्मथितं शिरः ।\nवृक्षात्फलमिवोद्धृत्य लगुडेन प्रमाथिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today I will strike your head off with a razor-edged arrow, as one knocks a fruit from a tree with a pounding club.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा महाराज सहदेवो महाबलः ।\nसंक्रुद्धो नरशार्दूलो वेगेनाभिजगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken so, the mighty Sahadeva, a tiger among men, enraged, went swiftly at him."}},{"n":51,"text":"अभिगम्य तु दुर्धर्षः सहदेवो युधां पतिः ।\nविकृष्य बलवच्चापं क्रोधेन प्रहसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Approaching, the unassailable Sahadeva, lord of warriors, drew his strong bow and, as if laughing in his anger,"}},{"n":52,"text":"शकुनिं दशभिर्विद्ध्वा चतुर्भिश्चास्य वाजिनः ।\nछत्रं ध्वजं धनुश्चास्य छित्त्वा सिंह इवानदत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"pierced Shakuni with ten arrows and his horses with four, cut his parasol, banner and bow, and roared like a lion."}},{"n":53,"text":"छिन्नध्वजधनुश्छत्रः सहदेवेन सौबलः ।\nततो विद्धश्च बहुभिः सर्वमर्मसु सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his banner, bow and parasol cut by Sahadeva, Shakuni, son of Subala, was then pierced in all his vital parts with many arrows."}},{"n":54,"text":"ततो भूयो महाराज सहदेवः प्रतापवान् ।\nशकुनेः प्रेषयामास शरवृष्टिं दुरासदाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then again, O great king, the mighty Sahadeva sent an irresistible shower of arrows at Shakuni."}},{"n":55,"text":"ततस्तु क्रुद्धः सुबलस्य पुत्रो\nमाद्रीसुतं सहदेवं विमर्दे ।\nप्रासेन जाम्बूनदभूषणेन\nजिघांसुरेकोऽभिपपात शीघ्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, angered, the son of Subala charged swiftly alone at Madri's son Sahadeva in the melee, wishing to kill him with a spear adorned with Jambunada gold."}},{"n":56,"text":"माद्रीसुतस्तस्य समुद्यतं तं\nप्रासं सुवृत्तौ च भुजौ रणाग्रे ।\nभल्लैस्त्रिभिर्युगपत्संचकर्त\nननाद चोच्चैस्तरसाजिमध्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the front of the battle, the son of Madri cut that raised spear and his well-rounded arms at one stroke with three broad-headed arrows, and roared loudly and swiftly in the midst of the fight."}},{"n":57,"text":"तस्याशुकारी सुसमाहितेन\nसुवर्णपुङ्खेन दृढायसेन ।\nभल्लेन सर्वावरणातिगेन\nशिरः शरीरात्प्रममाथ भूयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, working quickly, he struck off Shakuni's head from his body with a well-aimed, gold-feathered, hard-iron, broad-headed arrow that passes through all armor."}},{"n":58,"text":"शरेण कार्तस्वरभूषितेन\nदिवाकराभेन सुसंशितेन ।\nहृतोत्तमाङ्गो युधि पाण्डवेन\nपपात भूमौ सुबलस्य पुत्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a gold-adorned arrow, sharp, shining like the sun, the son of Subala, his head taken by the Pandava, fell to the ground in the battle."}},{"n":59,"text":"स तच्छिरो वेगवता शरेण\nसुवर्णपुङ्खेन शिलाशितेन ।\nप्रावेरयत्कुपितः पाण्डुपुत्रो\nयत्तत्कुरूणामनयस्य मूलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enraged, the son of Pandu then sent that head, the root of the Kurus' misfortune, flying with a swift, gold-feathered arrow whetted on stone."}},{"n":60,"text":"हृतोत्तमाङ्गं शकुनिं समीक्ष्य\nभूमौ शयानं रुधिरार्द्रगात्रम् ।\nयोधास्त्वदीया भयनष्टसत्त्वा\nदिशः प्रजग्मुः प्रगृहीतशस्त्राः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Shakuni lying on the ground, his head taken and his limbs wet with blood, your warriors, their courage lost in fear, fled in all directions with weapons in hand."}},{"n":61,"text":"विप्रद्रुताः शुष्कमुखा विसंज्ञा\nगाण्डीवघोषेण समाहताश्च ।\nभयार्दिता भग्नरथाश्वनागाः\nपदातयश्चैव सधार्तराष्ट्राः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Routed, with dry mouths and out of their senses, struck by the roar of the Gandiva, tormented by fear, with chariots, horses and elephants broken, the foot soldiers fled, and the Dhartarashtras too."}},{"n":62,"text":"ततो रथाच्छकुनिं पातयित्वा\nमुदान्विता भारत पाण्डवेयाः ।\nशङ्खान्प्रदध्मुः समरे प्रहृष्टाः\nसकेशवाः सैनिकान्हर्षयन्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having felled Shakuni from his chariot, the Pandavas, O Bharata, full of joy, blew their conches in the battle with Keshava, gladdening their soldiers."}},{"n":63,"text":"तं चापि सर्वे प्रतिपूजयन्तो\nहृष्टा ब्रुवाणाः सहदेवमाजौ ।\nदिष्ट्या हतो नैकृतिको दुरात्मा\nसहात्मजो वीर रणे त्वयेति ॥","meaning":{"en":"All of them, rejoicing, honored Sahadeva in the battle, saying, \"By good fortune, hero, the deceitful, wicked man has been killed by you in the battle, with his son!\""}}]}]}